--- !u!114 &2478113021727359127
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 6214952312162754950}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "\tRichard Funderburg took on the role only two years ago, with hefty promises
    to oversee the renovation of homeland naval architecture to accommodate the expansion
    of naval military operations. His most recent project involved the Puget Sound
    Naval Shipyard, which is expected to see employment growth of up to 200% by the
    end of this year. According to local sources, construction had frequently been
    delayed or halted, and Funderburg announced in October that he would be personally
    visiting the site with the intention to \u201Cenforce compliance for the good
    of the safety of the American people.\u201D \r\n\tPassengers on an early-morning
    ferry from Bremerton to Seattle alerted police to what appeared to be a body
    floating in the Sinclair Inlet, and police quickly recovered and identified the
    corpse. Funderburg\u2019s hotel room was searched, yielding nothing out of the
    ordinary, but his car was discovered near PSNS, with both front doors unlocked
    and with severe bloodstaining in the driver\u2019s seat and carpet. It is unclear
    whether Funderburg was alive when he entered the inlet, and no further details
    have been made available as to the cause of death or potential agitators. \r\n\tWithout
    Funderburg\u2019s initiative, inside sources say it is unlikely that his projects
    at PSNS will move forward.\r\n\r\n\tThis story is still developing. \n\n\xA9
    Seattle Times, 2002\nAuthor Kevin DuBois"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0445602e006599347a14a022e954282d, type: 2}
